<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-tag">Common questions</span>
      <h2>The important details, before you install.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>Does WhatBattery change how my Mac charges?</h3><p>No. It is strictly read-only. It reads battery and power data through Apple's interfaces and never writes to the battery, enforces a charge limit, or changes charging behaviour.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>Why is it not in the Mac App Store?</h3><p>The App Sandbox blocks the low-level IOKit and SMC reads WhatBattery needs. It ships directly as a Developer ID-signed and Apple-notarised app, so it opens without a Gatekeeper warning.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>How does the iPhone and iPad reading work?</h3><p>Trust the Mac once over a cable, then read the device over USB or Wi-Fi using the same connection Finder uses. No app is installed on the device. <a href="/docs/iphone-ipad/">Read the setup guide.</a></p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h3>What does Pro cost?</h3><p>£9.99 once, for up to two Macs. There is no subscription and purchases have a 14-day money-back guarantee.</p></div>
    </div>
